    <!-- Legal -->
    <string name="legal_licenses_intro">Aura is built with these open-source components. Tap one to read its license.</string>
    <string name="legal_privacy_body">## Overview\n\nAura is designed to keep your information on your device. There are no accounts, no advertising and no analytics or tracking SDKs.\n\n## Data stored on your device\n\nYour name, profile picture, country, tasks, reminders, Quick Apps and preferences are stored only in Aura\'s private storage on your phone. The most recent news headlines are cached so they are available offline.\n\n## Network requests\n\nTo show news, Aura downloads headlines directly from the news publishers\' public RSS feeds or, if configured by the app\'s distributor, from the NewsData.io news service. Article images are loaded from the publishers\' servers. These requests include standard technical information such as your IP address and the app name, as with any web request. Your tasks, reminders, name and other personal data are never sent.\n\n## Installed apps\n\nTo let you pin and open apps, Aura reads the list of launchable apps installed on your device. This list is used only on your device and is never uploaded.\n\n## Permissions\n\nNotifications are used only to deliver the reminders and task alerts you create. \"Alarms &amp; reminders\" lets reminders fire at the exact minute. Internet and network-state access are used to load news and to show when you are offline. Starting at boot lets Aura restore your reminders after the phone restarts.\n\n## Backups\n\nIf Android device backup is enabled, Android may include Aura\'s data in your encrypted Google backup so it can be restored on a new phone. Temporary caches, such as article images, are excluded.\n\n## Deleting your data\n\nDelete individual items in the app, or remove everything by clearing Aura\'s storage in Android Settings or uninstalling the app.\n\n## Changes\n\nIf this policy changes, the updated version will be included with the app update.</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_body">## Using Aura\n\nAura is a personal productivity dashboard provided free of charge and \"as is\", without warranties of any kind.\n\n## Reminders\n\nAura schedules reminders using Android\'s alarm system. Battery-saving features, manufacturer restrictions or disabled notifications can delay or prevent alerts. Don\'t rely on Aura for critical or safety-related alerts.\n\n## News content\n\nHeadlines, summaries and images belong to their respective publishers and are shown with attribution to the original source. Tapping an article opens it on the publisher\'s own website, where the publisher\'s terms apply. Aura does not create, edit or verify news content.\n\n## Third-party apps\n\nQuick Apps opens apps installed on your device. Those apps are provided by their developers and are governed by their own terms.\n\n## Liability\n\nTo the extent permitted by law, the developers of Aura are not liable for any loss resulting from the use of the app, including missed reminders or lost data.</string>
